This is the original proposal for extending the DWARF standard:
https://dwarfstd.org/issues/100831.1.html

The PDF file "DWARF5 implicit ptrs only.pdf" contains pages from the
actual DWARF standard, to which we must conform.

The file "gdb-implicit-ptrs.patch" contains the diff for supporting
implicit pointers in the gdb debugger, which can be used for reference.

One of the main ideas is that you have to be able to distinguish in
the debugger between:
1. pointers to memory in the target program being debugged (this is the normal case);
2. implicit pointers, which are pointers to memory in the *debugger's* address
space, where we are going to conjure up values based on descriptions in the
DWARF associated with the given executable.

